---
const features = [
  {
    icon: "🤖",
    title: "Agent orchestration",
    description:
      "Vera decomposes complex tasks into subtasks handled by specialized agents — a research agent gathers context, a planning agent structures the work, and an execution agent writes code. Each agent has access to the tools it needs: file system, web search, GitHub API, Linear API.",
  },
  {
    icon: "🧠",
    title: "Codebase understanding",
    description:
      "Before writing code, Vera reads your repository. She traces data flows, identifies patterns, maps dependencies, and understands your conventions — so the code she writes looks like your team wrote it.",
  },
  {
    icon: "🔄",
    title: "Structured workflows",
    description:
      "Every task follows a deterministic workflow with checkpoints, approval gates, and crash-safe state. Vera doesn't hallucinate a plan and hope for the best — she follows the same engineering process your team already uses.",
  },
];
---

<section
  id="architecture"
  class="architecture"
  aria-labelledby="arch-heading"
>
  <div class="section-inner">
    <h2 id="arch-heading">How Vera works under the hood</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      Vera isn't a wrapper around an LLM. She's a multi-agent system with
      persistent memory, tool access, and structured workflows.
    </p>

    <div class="arch-grid">
      {
        features.map((f) => (
          <div class="arch-card">
            <div class="arch-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              {f.icon}
            </div>
            <h3>{f.title}</h3>
            <p>{f.description}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <div class="byok-banner">
      <div class="byok-icon" aria-hidden="true">🔑</div>
      <div class="byok-content">
        <h3>Your keys, your models</h3>
        <p>
          Vera supports BYOK (bring your own key) — use your preferred LLM
          provider. Your code stays in your infrastructure. Nothing is stored or
          used for training.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .architecture {
    padding: 5rem 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(13, 40, 24, 0.15);
  }

  .section-inner {
    max-width: var(--max-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .section-intro {
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto 3rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .arch-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .arch-card {
    padding: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(13, 40, 24, 0.15);
    border-radius: 16px;
    transition: border-color 0.2s, transform 0.2s;
  }

  .arch-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-text);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .arch-icon {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 52px;
    height: 52px;
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .arch-card p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .byok-banner {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(13, 40, 24, 0.15);
    border-radius: 16px;
  }

  .byok-icon {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 64px;
    height: 64px;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }

  .byok-content h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .byok-content p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .arch-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .byok-banner {
      flex-direction: column;
      text-align: center;
    }
  }
</style>
